s and a note counting ads without a reliable location match and so absent from the map. Submitting the form moves the whole results view upward from below the screen over 1.2 seconds while the background gradient rotates steadily at 150 degrees per second, with the form visible behind it until the movement finishes. Reduced-motion preferences skip the visible movement. Verified on 8 November 2026 in commit `Speed up gradient rotation during results transition`: desktop and 390-by-844 mobile browser checks showed the gradient turning 60 degrees after 400 milliseconds, a 1.2-second slide, no horizontal overflow, and both animations removed when the results settled. Edit restores the original gradient. Reduced motion disabled rotation, and the browser had no console errors. Web lint, typecheck and build passed. The results fill the window: the map fills the left two thirds and stays in view while the column scrolls in the right third, and on phones the map sits on top at 55% of the screen height. Verified on 7 November 2026 in commit `Animate results upward after form submission`: desktop and 390-by-844 mobile browser checks confirmed that the results and their content move together, settle at the top without horizontal overflow, and preserve the form answers on Edit. Reduced motion completed immediately, invalid amounts blocked submission, and the browser had no console errors. Web lint, typecheck and build passed. The column opens with a one-line summary of the brief and an Edit button that brings the form back with its answers kept. Submitting a completely empty form runs the sample fintech budgeting-app brief with a $3,000 monthly budget in New York. Entering any field or changing a dropdown keeps full required-field and numeric-pattern validation. There is no separate `/map` route. Verified on 7 November 2026 in commit `Use sample defaults for empty form submissions`: a blank submission showed the sample map and 12 placements; each individually filled field and a 